{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-psalms-078",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 78,
  "title": "Psalms 78",
  "display_title": "Psalms 78",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 78,
  "sortOrder": 19078,
  "verseCount": 72,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Give ear, O my people, to my law: incline your ears to the words of my mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "I will open my mouth in a parable: I will utter dark sayings of old:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Which we have heard and known, and our fathers have told us.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "We will not hide them from their children, shewing to the generation to come the praises of the LORD, and his strength, and his wonderful works that he hath done.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For he established a testimony in Jacob, and appointed a law in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, that they should make them known to their children:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "That the generation to come might know them, even the children which should be born; who should arise and declare them to their children:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "That they might set their hope in God, and not forget the works of God, but keep his commandments:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And might not be as their fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation; a generation that set not their heart aright, and whose spirit was not stedfast with God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "The children of Ephraim, being armed, and carrying bows, turned back in the day of battle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "They kept not the covenant of God, and refused to walk in his law;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And forgat his works, and his wonders that he had shewed them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Marvellous things did he in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the field of Zoan.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "He divided the sea, and caused them to pass through; and he made the waters to stand as an heap.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "In the daytime also he led them with a cloud, and all the night with a light of fire.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "He clave the rocks in the wilderness, and gave them drink as out of the great depths.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "He brought streams also out of the rock, and caused waters to run down like rivers.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And they sinned yet more against him by provoking the most High in the wilderness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And they tempted God in their heart by asking meat for their lust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Yea, they spake against God; they said, Can God furnish a table in the wilderness?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Behold, he smote the rock, that the waters gushed out, and the streams overflowed; can he give bread also? can he provide flesh for his people?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Therefore the LORD heard this, and was wroth: so a fire was kindled against Jacob, and anger also came up against Israel;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Because they believed not in God, and trusted not in his salvation:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Though he had commanded the clouds from above, and opened the doors of heaven,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "And had rained down manna upon them to eat, and had given them of the corn of heaven.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Man did eat angels’ food: he sent them meat to the full.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "He caused an east wind to blow in the heaven: and by his power he brought in the south wind.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "He rained flesh also upon them as dust, and feathered fowls like as the sand of the sea:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "And he let it fall in the midst of their camp, round about their habitations.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "So they did eat, and were well filled: for he gave them their own desire;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "They were not estranged from their lust. But while their meat was yet in their mouths,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "The wrath of God came upon them, and slew the fattest of them, and smote down the chosen men of Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "For all this they sinned still, and believed not for his wondrous works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Therefore their days did he consume in vanity, and their years in trouble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "When he slew them, then they sought him: and they returned and enquired early after God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "And they remembered that God was their rock, and the high God their redeemer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "Nevertheless they did flatter him with their mouth, and they lied unto him with their tongues.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "For their heart was not right with him, neither were they stedfast in his covenant.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "But he, being full of compassion, forgave their iniquity, and destroyed them not: yea, many a time turned he his anger away, and did not stir up all his wrath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "For he remembered that they were but flesh; a wind that passeth away, and cometh not again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-040",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 40,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:40",
      "numberLabel": "40",
      "text": "How oft did they provoke him in the wilderness, and grieve him in the desert!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:40",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:40"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-041",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 41,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:41",
      "numberLabel": "41",
      "text": "Yea, they turned back and tempted God, and limited the Holy One of Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:41",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-042",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 42,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:42",
      "numberLabel": "42",
      "text": "They remembered not his hand, nor the day when he delivered them from the enemy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:42",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:42"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-043",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 43,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:43",
      "numberLabel": "43",
      "text": "How he had wrought his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Zoan:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:43",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-044",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 44,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:44",
      "numberLabel": "44",
      "text": "And had turned their rivers into blood; and their floods, that they could not drink.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:44",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:44"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-045",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 45,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:45",
      "numberLabel": "45",
      "text": "He sent divers sorts of flies among them, which devoured them; and frogs, which destroyed them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:45",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:45"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-046",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 46,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:46",
      "numberLabel": "46",
      "text": "He gave also their increase unto the caterpiller, and their labour unto the locust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:46",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:46"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-047",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 47,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:47",
      "numberLabel": "47",
      "text": "He destroyed their vines with hail, and their sycomore trees with frost.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:47",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:47"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-048",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 48,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:48",
      "numberLabel": "48",
      "text": "He gave up their cattle also to the hail, and their flocks to hot thunderbolts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:48",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-049",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 49,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:49",
      "numberLabel": "49",
      "text": "He cast upon them the fierceness of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and trouble, by sending evil angels among them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:49",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:49"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-050",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 50,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:50",
      "numberLabel": "50",
      "text": "He made a way to his anger; he spared not their soul from death, but gave their life over to the pestilence;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:50",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:50"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-051",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 51,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:51",
      "numberLabel": "51",
      "text": "And smote all the firstborn in Egypt; the chief of their strength in the tabernacles of Ham:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:51",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-052",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 52,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:52",
      "numberLabel": "52",
      "text": "But made his own people to go forth like sheep, and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:52",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:52"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-053",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 53,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:53",
      "numberLabel": "53",
      "text": "And he led them on safely, so that they feared not: but the sea overwhelmed their enemies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:53",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-054",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 54,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:54",
      "numberLabel": "54",
      "text": "And he brought them to the border of his sanctuary, even to this mountain, which his right hand had purchased.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:54",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:54"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-055",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 55,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:55",
      "numberLabel": "55",
      "text": "He cast out the heathen also before them, and divided them an inheritance by line, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:55",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-056",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 56,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:56",
      "numberLabel": "56",
      "text": "Yet they tempted and provoked the most high God, and kept not his testimonies:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:56",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:56"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-057",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 57,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:57",
      "numberLabel": "57",
      "text": "But turned back, and dealt unfaithfully like their fathers: they were turned aside like a deceitful bow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:57",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:57"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-058",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 58,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:58",
      "numberLabel": "58",
      "text": "For they provoked him to anger with their high places, and moved him to jealousy with their graven images.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:58",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:58"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-059",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 59,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:59",
      "numberLabel": "59",
      "text": "When God heard this, he was wroth, and greatly abhorred Israel:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:59",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:59"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-060",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 60,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:60",
      "numberLabel": "60",
      "text": "So that he forsook the tabernacle of Shiloh, the tent which he placed among men;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:60",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:60"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-061",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 61,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:61",
      "numberLabel": "61",
      "text": "And delivered his strength into captivity, and his glory into the enemy’s hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:61",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:61"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-062",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 62,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:62",
      "numberLabel": "62",
      "text": "He gave his people over also unto the sword; and was wroth with his inheritance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:62",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:62"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-063",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 63,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:63",
      "numberLabel": "63",
      "text": "The fire consumed their young men; and their maidens were not given to marriage.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:63",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:63"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-064",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 64,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:64",
      "numberLabel": "64",
      "text": "Their priests fell by the sword; and their widows made no lamentation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:64",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:64"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-065",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 65,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:65",
      "numberLabel": "65",
      "text": "Then the LORD awaked as one out of sleep, and like a mighty man that shouteth by reason of wine.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:65",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:65"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-066",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 66,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:66",
      "numberLabel": "66",
      "text": "And he smote his enemies in the hinder parts: he put them to a perpetual reproach.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:66",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:66"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-067",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 67,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:67",
      "numberLabel": "67",
      "text": "Moreover he refused the tabernacle of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of Ephraim:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:67",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:67"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-068",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 68,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:68",
      "numberLabel": "68",
      "text": "But chose the tribe of Judah, the mount Zion which he loved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:68",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:68"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-069",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 69,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:69",
      "numberLabel": "69",
      "text": "And he built his sanctuary like high palaces, like the earth which he hath established for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:69",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:69"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-070",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 70,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:70",
      "numberLabel": "70",
      "text": "He chose David also his servant, and took him from the sheepfolds:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:70",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:70"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-071",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 71,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:71",
      "numberLabel": "71",
      "text": "From following the ewes great with young he brought him to feed Jacob his people, and Israel his inheritance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:71",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:71"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-072",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 72,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:78:72",
      "numberLabel": "72",
      "text": "So he fed them according to the integrity of his heart; and guided them by the skilfulness of his hands.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 78:72",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:78:72"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
